  "title": "Genyornis Extinction",
  "summary": "Genyornis newtoni, a large flightless Australian bird, disappeared after humans arrived. Burnt eggshell fragments at more than 200 sites, dated by three methods to 53.9–43.4 ka and likely before 47 ka, indicate people cooked its eggs. A 2016 study argued that egg harvesting contributed to its extinction.",
